From: nekochigura maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Build against system libraries instead of vendored downloads

Point onnxruntime's FetchContent declarations at system packages and mark the
system lookups REQUIRED, so the build fails loudly instead of silently
downloading a bundled copy.

Rebased onto 1.29.0 from the 1.27.0 patch: upstream reworked the Windows
ARM64/ARM64EC cpuinfo branch's PATCH_COMMAND (added
patches/cpuinfo/patch_cpuinfo_h_for_arm64ec.patch, dropped
win_arm_fp16_detection_fallback.patch), which stranded the hunk adding REQUIRED
to that branch. Only that hunk's context changed; the two REQUIRED additions
and every other edit are carried over unchanged.
--- a/cmake/external/abseil-cpp.cmake
+++ b/cmake/external/abseil-cpp.cmake
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@
     URL_HASH SHA1=${DEP_SHA1_abseil_cpp}
     EXCLUDE_FROM_ALL
     PATCH_COMMAND ${ABSL_PATCH_COMMAND}
-    FIND_PACKAGE_ARGS 20250814 NAMES absl
+    FIND_PACKAGE_ARGS NAMES absl REQUIRED
 )
 
 onnxruntime_fetchcontent_makeavailable(abseil_cpp)
